{"id":"zip-0233","number":233,"title":"Network Sustainability Mechanism: Removing Funds From Circulation","status":"Draft","statusDetail":null,"category":"Consensus / Ecosystem","owners":["Jason McGee","Zooko Wilcox","Mark Henderson","Tomek Piotrowski","Mariusz Pilarek","Paul Dann"],"created":"2023-08-16","license":"BSD-2-Clause","discussionsTo":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/issues/922","pullRequest":null,"kind":"zip","format":"md","source":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/blob/main/zips/zip-0233.md","official":"https://zips.z.cash/zip-0233","updatedAt":"2026-10-16T01:56:36Z","summary":"This ZIP proposes the introduction of a mechanism to voluntarily remove funds entirely from circulation on the network. The explicit intent of this removal is that the funds will be returned to circulation through future block subsidies,…","words":1102,"digest":"790e204072833060eae5e7cb2563acc23394a17680b6ce48eb602b713dc65d53","headings":[{"id":"terminology","title":"Terminology","level":2},{"id":"abstract","title":"Abstract","level":2},{"id":"motivation","title":"Motivation","level":2},{"id":"privacy-implications","title":"Privacy Implications","level":2},{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","level":2},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","level":2},{"id":"changes-to-zip-248","title":"Changes to ZIP 248","level":3},{"id":"nsm-amount","title":"NSM Amount","level":3},{"id":"changes-to-zip-237","title":"Changes to ZIP 237","level":3},{"id":"changes-to-the-zcash-protocol-specification","title":"Changes to the Zcash Protocol Specification","level":3},{"id":"modifications-to-digest-algorithms","title":"Modifications to Digest Algorithms","level":3},{"id":"applicability","title":"Applicability","level":3},{"id":"rationale","title":"Rationale","level":2},{"id":"new-transaction-field-for-amount-to-remove-from-circulation","title":"New transaction field for amount to remove from circulation","level":3},{"id":"deployment","title":"Deployment","level":2},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key word \"MUST\" in this document is to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"href":"#fn:BCP14"}],"id":"fnref:BCP14"}," when, and only when, it appears in all capitals."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The term \"network upgrade\" in this document is to be interpreted as described in ZIP 200. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"href":"#fn:zip-0200"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0200"}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The character § is used when referring to sections of the Zcash Protocol Specification. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"href":"#fn:protocol"}],"id":"fnref:protocol"}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The terms \"Mainnet\" and \"Testnet\" are to be interpreted as described in § 3.12 ‘Mainnet and Testnet’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"href":"#fn:protocol-networks"}],"id":"fnref:protocol-networks"}]},{"tag":"p","children":["\"ZEC/TAZ\" refers to the native currency of Zcash on a given network, i.e. ZEC on Mainnet and TAZ on Testnet."]},{"tag":"p","children":["\"Block Subsidy\" - The algorithmic issuance of ZEC/TAZ on block creation, as defined by consensus. This is split between the miner and Funding Streams."]},{"tag":"p","children":["\"Issuance\" - The method by which ZEC/TAZ becomes available for circulation on the network. [TODO: there is a potential terminology conflict between this and issuance as defined in ZIP 227.]"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖷"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖸"]}]}]},", as defined in § 5.3 ‘Constants’ ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"href":"#fn:protocol-constants"}],"id":"fnref:protocol-constants"},", is the total ZEC/TAZ supply cap measured in zatoshi, corresponding to 21,000,000 ZEC. This is slightly larger than the supply cap for the current issuance mechanism, but is the value used in existing critical consensus checks."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP proposes the introduction of a mechanism to voluntarily remove funds entirely from circulation on the network. The explicit intent of this removal is that the funds will be returned to circulation through future block subsidies, rather than being permanently destroyed or held in reserve for discretionary use. This mechanism, in combination with ZIPs 235 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"href":"#fn:zip-0235"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0235"}," and 237 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"href":"#fn:zip-0237"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0237"},", comprises a long-term strategy for the sustainability of the network. We will refer to the combined effects of these three ZIPs as the “Network Sustainability Mechanism”."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["This mechanism seeks to address concerns about the sustainability of the network design shared by Bitcoin-like systems:"]},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Long Term Consensus Sustainability:"]}," By enabling the removal of funds from circulation, the network gains the ability to create \"headroom\" between the chain value and ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖷"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖸"]}]}]},". This lays necessary groundwork for extending the block subsidy system, which currently has a clear final end date. The intent is that removed funds will be automatically and algorithmically reissued through future block subsidies, sustaining the network's long-term security budget, whether or not all three ZIPs comprising the Network Sustainability Mechanism are deployed in the same network upgrade."]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Benefits to ZEC Holders:"]}," Removing funds from circulation reduces the circulating supply of ZEC. To the extent that this potentially contributes to an increase in the value of remaining ZEC, it can be argued to benefit network users in proportion to their holdings — without requiring them to opt into any scheme, introducing extra risk, active oversight, or accounting complexity."]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Privacy Implications"],"id":"privacy-implications"},{"tag":"p","children":["ZIP 233 adds a new type of transparent transaction event that is fully visible to chain observers, and linked to other events performed in the transaction. The removal of funds from circulation does represent a potential distinguisher; transactions that intentionally remove funds from circulation are likely to represent a small fraction of Zcash transactions, and so this will provide another tool that adversaries may use to be able to segment users of the network."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Requirements"],"id":"requirements"},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["The mechanism enables users to remove funds from the circulating supply, and each removal event is explicitly specified in the corresponding transaction."]},{"tag":"li","children":["The process is publicly auditable, allowing network participants to verify the amount and occurrence of funds removed from circulation."]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Changes to ZIP 248"],"id":"changes-to-zip-248"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP proposes to register bundle type 6 variant 0 (\"ZIP 233 NSM field\") in the V7 transaction bundle type registry defined in ZIP 248 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"href":"#fn:zip-0248"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0248"},"."]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":["BundleType"]},{"tag":"th","children":["BundleVariant"]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["mValuePoolDeltas"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["mEffectBundles"]}]},{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["mAuthBundles"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["6"]},{"tag":"td","children":["0"]},{"tag":"td","children":["✅"]},{"tag":"td","children":["❌"]},{"tag":"td","children":["❌"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The NSM bundle has no effecting data and no authorizing data. The amount to be removed from circulation is represented solely as an entry in ",{"tag":"code","children":["mValuePoolDeltas"]}," with ",{"tag":"code","children":["bundleType = 6"]}," and ",{"tag":"code","children":["assetClass = 0"]}," (ZEC)."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["NSM Amount"],"id":"nsm-amount"},{"tag":"p","children":["When the ",{"tag":"code","children":["mValuePoolDeltas"]}," map contains an entry with ",{"tag":"code","children":["bundleType = 6"]},", the transaction removes funds from circulation. The entry's ",{"tag":"code","children":["value"]}," field MUST be nonpositive; its negation is denoted ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗓"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["𝟤𝟥𝟥"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗆"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]}]}]}," and represents the value in zatoshis removed from circulation when the transaction is mined. If no such entry is present, ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗓"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["𝟤𝟥𝟥"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗆"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]}]}]}," is defined to be 0."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The NSM bundle's effect on the transparent transaction value pool does not reflect an output being produced in any chain value pool. At the point at which the transaction is applied to the global chain state, ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗓"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["𝟤𝟥𝟥"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗆"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]}]}]}," is subtracted from the issued supply. It is unavailable for circulation on the network at least through to the end of the block in which the transaction is mined."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Changes to ZIP 237"],"id":"changes-to-zip-237"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP proposes to register the following mechanism for removal from circulation in the list defined in ZIP 237 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"href":"#fn:zip-0237"}],"id":"fnref2:zip-0237"},":"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":["Mechanism"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Source"]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["Transaction field"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖥"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},